Subject: SUMMARY: Patching Question
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653647622192

Several people responded.  Appearently /usr/sys/BINARY/files has a 
redundant definition for the 'ee' module.  Deleting the lines 
(leaving the file empty), and then redoing 'doconfig' solved the 
problem.

Originally I got the following errors, when compiling the kernel:
>  Configuration file has errors.
>  /usr/sys/BINARY/files: Local file MODULE/STATIC/ee overrides ee.
>  Error: module ee already exists

Here's one of the responses.

At 16:08 -0400 5/29/01, Dr. Thomas.Blinn@Compaq.com wrote:
>There are two files, /usr/sys/BINARY/files and /usr/sys/BINARY/alpha/files ,
>that have redundant definitions for the "ee" module.  Remove the references
>from one of the two files.  NHD3 put the references in one file, the patch
>kit put them in the other file, someone didn't realize they were done in two
>different places (the patch team engineer never checked how it was supposed
>to be done and got it wrong), and the testing was never done on a system
>with the new Ethernet module so it didn't get caught.
