From tru64-unix-managers  Wed May 30 08:07:24 2001
From: Lars Bro <Lars.Bro () gnnettest ! com>
Date: Wed, 30 May 2001 08:07:24 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: DVD
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653647622181

A disappointing experience.

1) There is no supported DVD device.

2) There is no real support for UDF on Tru64.

3) There is no support for boot on UDF (xxboot.udf)

Tom Blinn suggested that I place a UFS file system on the DVD instead.  This
is much more likely to boot, mount and everything. A nice idea, actually.
But anyway, with no supported hardware, there is no point in doing this.

Thomas Leitner got a 2 Gb Toshiba external SCSI DVD device running. I would
expect 4.7 Gb as far as I can see from Toshibas home page.

Yours,
Lars Bro

