From tru64-unix-managers  Wed May 30 06:44:01 2001
From: jasper Hoon <jasperhoon () webmail ! co ! za>
Date: Wed, 30 May 2001 06:44:01 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: Memory fault (Coredump) with pswd validation program
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653647622179

The problem was indeed with the incorrect passing of arguments.

Many thanks to the following people who sent information as well as
replacement code!

Stanislav S. Anokhin <stas@peterstar.com>
Dr. Thomas.Blinn@Compaq.com <tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com>
<LHERCAUD@bouyguestelecom.fr>
James Sainsbury <sainsb_j@chem.usyd.edu.au>
Jeff Sullivan <jps@zk3.dec.com>
Ann Majeske <Ann.Majeske@compaq.com>
Roetman, Paul <PRoetman@CSXLines.com>

The correct way is shown here:
===========
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <prot.h>
#include <sia.h>
#include <siad.h>
main (int argc, char *argv[])
{
      int auth_status;
      int myargc;
      char *myargv[2];

      myargc = 1;
      myargv[0] = "chkpass";
      myargv[1] = NULL;

auth_status=sia_validate_user(NULL,myargc,myargv,NULL,argv[1],
NULL,0,NULL , argv[2]);

      if( auth_status != SIASUCCESS){
              printf("wrong password \n");
              return(1);
      }
      printf("right password \n");
      return 0;
}
==============
