All,

Thanks to:
Ram Rao
Jim Barriault
Dr John Halewood
and Chris Bryant

Who all gave the answer along the same lines (different ways of getting the
output for the bus,target and lun) but (using Ram's answer)

Use "hwmgr -show scsi" to get a table mapping dsk? to bus/target/lun (shown
in First Valid Path column).

The console names devices on bus 0 dka??, on bus 1 dkb?? and so on.  The
target and lun are encoded as follows: (target*100) + lun.  So for example,
a bus/target/lun  of 2/3/5 would appear on the console of DKC305.


Thanks for the quick replies.

Steve

---------------------------------------

