Subject: SUMMARY: Hardware Swap on V5.1
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653647621990

     This swap went off without a hitch. All the cpus/memoryboards/HBA's 
     and NIC cards were brought over from the source 4100 and put into the 
     new 4100. Since it was all completely SCSI there were no "wwidmgr" 
     problems. All I did was make sure that my SCSI ID's were the same and 
     that my "show dev" at the POO>>> prompt matched up with the older 
     system. Then I did a "b -fl s -fi genvmunix" and rebuilt the kernel. 
     The only device that changed device special file names on me was the 
     cd-rom. A quick "sum /vmunix /vmunix.old" showed a very slight change 
     in the kernel as well. Thanks to everyone who tried to help with 
     suggestions especially the ones with the confident "I bet it will 
     work" messages, 
     
