To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Tru64 UNIX V5.1 patch kit 3 status
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653647621989

Since there seems to be some concern about the current status of the
patch kit, here is the latest information.  The patch kit is on hold 
for the following reason:

> There is nothing wrong with the contents of the
> patch kit. However, a problem has been discovered with the baselining
> feature of the dupatch installation tool in which it does not
> operate properly.     A situation has been discovered in dupatch
> that disables the ability  to enable patches for installation once
> conflicts are found during the baseline process. The symptom of the
> problem is that conflicts between the patch kit and installed software
> are found as expected, however the user is not given the ability to
> enable patches for installation in phase 5 of the baseline process.  In
> phase 5 of baselining, it will show that no patches with file
> applicability conflicts are detected, however, in previous phases of
> baselining, conflicts were encounterd.  This mainly affects customers
> with manually installed patches and wants to overwrite them with the
> contents of the patch kit.  If you have successfully installed this
> patch kit, then this problem will have no effect on your system.

I do not have any further information, such as when the replacement kit
will be available, at this time.

Martin
