     Even though we haven't resolved all our V5.1 issues on our GS320's 
     yet, we have managed to get multipathing working finally. We were not 
     able to failover from one path to the other previously. After applying 
     Patch Kit 3, we had to apply a couple of point patches 
     1. Patch to fix "malloc_internal" panics
     2. CFS relocate patch
     
     Also, We updated the KGPSA driver version to V1.29a(Patch Kit 3 gives 
     you this). The cpu firmware was updated V5.9B, the KGPSA firmware was 
     updated to DS381A4, the HSG80's firmware was updated to V8.5F - 4 and 
     finally the brocade switch firmware was updated to V2.1.9G.
     
     
     One important lesson that we learnt while trying to make multipathing 
     work in our storage setup - If you have a pair of HSG80's configured 
     for dual redundancy and you are using only two ports out of the 4 on 
     the pair, try and use port 1 on both of them. We were using port 1 on 
     the A controller and port 2 on the B controller and although a lot of 
     people said that this should not be a problem, it was ultimately the 
     one change that allowed multipathing to work as designed. We still 
     have some outstanding issues with "invalid config for cluster seq 
     disk" panics and cnxmgr panics. But at least multipathing seems to be 
     working now. We have tried dropping a controller out of a pair and 
     also a san switch and where before, everything used to panic, it fails 
     over quite well to the other path now.
     
     
