Subject: SUMMARY2: mt erase error on /dev/nrmt0h with 4mm tape drive	on 4.0F
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653647621854

Thanks to Dr. Blinn for additional information and another solution.

The "erase" command is not implemented for DAT tape drives, only QIC which =
arent' available for current systems running Tru64.

Suggestion:  Use  mt weof after an mt rewind.  A file set using 1 block =
will be placed each time you do this to the norewind device.  Keep track =
of how many times you do this to keep your restores correct.  This is much =
faster than the SCU mt erase. =20

