From tru64-unix-managers  Thu May 10 16:36:55 2001
From: "Aldridge, Robert E. \(Rob\)" <realdridge () mcdermott ! com>
Date: Thu, 10 May 2001 16:36:55 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: HSG60 Tru64 / SWCC
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653647621791


Thanks for all the answers/suggestions.

The Compaq support center came through with this "workaround""

Step 1. Remove all current SWCC software from the NT machine

Step 2. Install SWCC 2.1 (1999 version of software).  This is the old client
software on the Compaq web site at:
ftp://ftp.compaq.com/pub/products/storageworks/storage_mgmt/swccdown/swcc21x
86client.exe

Step 3. Install just the HSG60 client from the newer CD.  (HSG60 client,
v2.2).

Apparently the master console window in the newer 2.2 software does not work
(or doesn't work with the HSG60 module).  But the master console window from
the 2.1 release works; just add in the newer HSG60 client module.



Other helpful information I received from this mailing list:
- SWCC development lags behind; apparently developed by a third-party
- Check firmware version on the HSG60
- Check the agent setup on the Tru64 side; make sure the agent is configured
for the NT client; add the NT client to the Tru64 hosts file
- Use the command line!  The command line CLI was working fine from the NT
side, by the way.
- Thanks to this mailing list, I now know how to access the HSG60 CLI from
the Tru64 host system.
	 /usr/lbin/hxsterm5 -b1 -t0 -l0  (bus1 target0 lun0)

	

Rob Aldridge
AT&T Solutions
Alliance, Ohio

