eg., suppose a packet arrrives to nic2 (and is internally
routed through 192.55.15.1) will hit the router and of course
be dropped because of the source address mismatch.

I have read the archives and a lot talk about ifconfig using
multinet (alias), and routed etc. Both IPs need to be real and
not aliases. Basically, and I'm sure all of you have come accross
this problem, I need to construct the IP config of both cards
so that a packet inbound to nic1 leaves nic1 and a packet inbound
for nic2 leaves nic2.

Any hints, pointers?
Many thanks in advance.

