This list is the greatest!!!!


Original question:

> I've got a 4.0g system that I didn't do the installation on and I need to
> know which Kernel Options were installed during system installation.
> 
> How do I do that?

The definitive answer from Dr. Tom Blinn:

The ONLY way to know if no one kept a log is to look at the kernel
config file that was used to build the system.

Why not just use doconfig and select that SHOULD be there, then
compare the generated file to the current (backup) file? 


