Admins,

It appears to be a easy answer..

From: Pat Lampert

Install as follows:

1.Load the CD-ROM optical disc labeled Tru64 UNIX Associated Products
Volume 1 into the CD-ROM drive.

2.Make a directory to be the mount point of the CD-ROM and then mount
the CD-ROM by entering commands similar to the following:



# mkdir /cdrom

# mount -rd /dev/rz4c /cdrom

# cd /cdrom/Worldwide_Language_Support/kit



3.Invoke the wwinstall script to install Tru64 UNIX Worldwide Support
software subsets as shown in the following example:



# ./wwinstall


Select the Chinese variant(s) you want from the menu that appears.

and also From:  Debra LaGattuta

The Chinese Language software subsets are located
on the 4.0F Associated Products CD-ROM volume 1.

Mount the CD-ROM on the mount point of your
choice, and then use the setld -l command
to load the Chinese language software.

Here's a link to the V4.0F Installation Guide
if you need more information:

http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/faqs/publications/pub_page/V40F_DOCS.HTM



Thanks again for your help

Lee Brewer


