appreciated all your responses.</FONT></P>

<P><FONT SIZE=3D2>I went with the following commands to complete the =
backup of the necessary files I wanted.</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT SIZE=3D2>1. Copy textual control file</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2>find =
/d06/trace/* | tail -1&nbsp; &gt;&gt;backemup.dat</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>2. Write all prod files to backemup.dat</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2>find =
/d0[1234567]/oradata/prod -type f -print | grep -v 'archp' =
&gt;&gt;backemup.dat</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>3. Write all archive log files to =
backemup.dat</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2>ls =
/d06/oradata/prod/archive/*.ARC &gt;&gt;backemup.dat</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>4. Copy all files listed in backemup.dat to =
tape.</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2>cpio =
-ovC65536 &lt;backemup.dat&gt; /dev/rmt2h</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>5. Remove backemup.dat file when finished.</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2>rm =
backemup.dat</FONT>
<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>6. List contents of tape</FONT>
<BR>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <FONT SIZE=3D2>cpio =
-itvC65536 -I/dev/rmt2h</FONT>
</P>

